[N 36-37 Scarlet Monastery]
[D Forever Shaman 30-60 (Braedyn)\\From Nijel's Point to Southshore for Down the Scarlet Path, the Dalaran crater (Lan'dalock, Olvek) and the swim into Tirisfal, Scarlet Monastery's Library and Armory (the Cathedral waits for chapter 39c), then the crater and Ironforge, where chapter 35 picks up.]
[GA Alliance]
[OC]|cffffffffLevel check|r  -  This chapter wants level 36: In the Name of the Light and Down the Scarlet Path need 34, and the wings set the level. At 36 the Library (mobs 33-37) and the Armory (35-40, Herod 40 elite) suit a group of five. The Cathedral (37-42, Mograine and Whitemane 42 elite) is not run here: it waits for chapter 39c at level 39-40. Under 36: run the Library first (that is the order anyway) and find a group a level or two higher for the Armory; there is no earlier dungeon chapter to fall back on
[OC]|cffffffffNijel's Point|r  -  you start at Nijel's Point in Desolace; hearth = Nijel's Point and it stays there, unused (do not hearth on this trip: it would put you back in Desolace). Required chapter: one trip to the Eastern Kingdoms, two wings of the Scarlet Monastery, |cFFFF0000GROUP 5|r. Three quests, 7,950 XP and 45s, handed in here, plus the dungeon kills; In the Name of the Light (4,700 XP) is handed in in chapter 39c
[OC]|cffffcc00Log check:|r Down the Scarlet Path (1052, chapter 33), Mythology of the Titans (1050) and Past Due (96800) from chapter 27, Storm, Earth, and Fire (79358) and On the Lam (79235, chapter 37). The Coldbringer's Eye (96773) is picked up below: it needs level 34, so chapter 27 could not take it
[OC][A Shaman] No shaman trainer on this trip: chapter 35 trains at Eldrun in Ironforge, where this chapter ends
[OC]|cffffcc00Sources:|r quest ids, mob and boss levels, drops and item stats come from the Forever DB and the Wowhead Forever tooltips. Which wing holds which mobs and bosses, the wing portals and the Scarlet Key's doors are Classic knowledge, not verified on Forever; the DB has no positions inside the instance, so the pins on dungeon lines point at the courtyard

[OC]|cffffffffThe way in|r  -  the Auberdine flight, then the Auberdine boat, which in Forever carries on past Menethil to Southshore (chapter 08's boat; dock times unverified). About 20-25 minutes
At [TAR6706 Baritanas Skyriver], |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Auberdine]|r [G64.7,10.5 Desolace]
Cross the Auberdine dock and take the Menethil boat; stay on it through Menethil until it docks at Southshore [G33.5,40 Darkshore]
At [TAR3980 Raleigh the Devout], [QT1052] (1,550 XP) [QA1053 In the Name of the Light] (4,700 XP: kill Houndmaster Loksey, Herod, Scarlet Commander Mograine and High Inquisitor Whitemane in the Scarlet Monastery) [G51.5,58.4 Hillsbrad Foothills]

[OC]|cFFFF0000The trek north|r  -  chapter 08's route: north out of Southshore keeping WEST of the road (Tarren Mill in the north-east is a Horde town), across the Hillsbrad Fields, through the north-west pass into Alterac and down into the Dalaran crater
[OC][A Shaman] Ghost Wolf for the whole trek (outdoors only)
Run to the Hillsbrad Fields [G33,42 Hillsbrad Foothills]
Through the north-west pass to the Dalaran crater [G18,72 Alterac Mountains]
At [TAR20735 Archmage Lan'dalock], [QA96773 The Coldbringer's Eye] (4,100 XP + 55s, requires level 34: the Eye lies in Razorfen Downs - carried to chapter 39b, handed in back here in 39c) [G15.9,73.1 Alterac Mountains]
[OC]Swim from the Dalaran shore north across Lordamere Lake until the zone text says Tirisfal Glades, then cross Tirisfal north-east to the Monastery. This is Horde country: keep off the roads. Classic-era: the Scarlet courtyard holds level 30-31 Scarlet Sentries, Augurs and Disciples; the spirit healer for a wipe stands at 78.9,41.0 Tirisfal, south of the Meeting Stone
Swim north across Lordamere Lake and run north-east across Tirisfal, off the roads, to the Meeting Stone below the Monastery [G82.1,39.2 Tirisfal Glades]
[OC]|cffffcc00Entrance (unverified):|r the courtyard is at about 84,31 (the Scarlet mobs' spawns); an earlier note puts the wing portals at 82.6,33.8 Tirisfal, Classic knowledge. Four portals, one per wing: you want the Library, then the Armory; the Cathedral is chapter 39c's. The Graveyard wing (30-34) has nothing for you

[OC]|cffffffffScarlet Monastery|r  -  |cFFFF0000GROUP 5|r for every wing, one run per wing, never a re-run. Your quests, with the honest label:
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r In the Name of the Light (1053) - kill Houndmaster Loksey (Library), Herod (Armory), Scarlet Commander Mograine and High Inquisitor Whitemane (Cathedral) - |cff66ff66normal|r: four boss kills in three wings, Loksey and Herod here, Mograine and Whitemane in chapter 39c. 4,700 XP at Raleigh in Southshore, in chapter 39c
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Mythology of the Titans (1050) - a book lying in the Library - |cff66ff66normal|r: an object; the DB has no position for it inside. 3,550 XP at Librarian Mae Paledust in Ironforge
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Past Due (96800) - The Lost Magic of the Runemasters - |cff66ff66normal|r: also a book on the ground (Wowhead Forever: 191 of 191 loots from the object); its spot in the Library is unverified, so look along every hall. 2,850 XP + 45s at Magus Olvek in the crater
[OC]|cffffcc00The Scarlet Key|r (Classic: opens the Armory and Cathedral doors; unverified on Forever): it lies in Doan's Strongbox at the end of the Library, and Scarlet Diviners, Chaplains and Monks can drop it too. So the Library comes first; keep the Key in your bags for the Cathedral in chapter 39c

[OC]|cffffffffLibrary|r  -  mobs 33-37 in the DB: Gallants and Adepts 33-34, Beastmasters, Diviners and Chaplains 34-35, Monks 35-36; Houndmaster Loksey 34 elite with his dogs, Arcanist Doan 37 elite at the end
|cFFFF0000GROUP 5|r Meet the group and enter the Library wing [G83.9,31.3 Tirisfal Glades]
Kill [TAR3974 Houndmaster Loksey] [QC1053,4] [G83.9,31.3 Tirisfal Glades]
[OC]|cffffcc00Loot (Loksey):|r Dog Training Gloves (leather hands +24 attack power, +21 more against beasts, req 31, ~30%) - take them if nobody needs them: a tie with Seawolf Gloves in general, better on beasts. Loksey's Training Stick (staff) is below Defender of Dalaran - pass
Loot the Mythology of the Titans book where it lies in the Library [QC1050] [G83.9,31.3 Tirisfal Glades]
Loot The Lost Magic of the Runemasters book from the ground (spot unverified) [QC96800] [G83.9,31.3 Tirisfal Glades]
Kill [TAR6487 Arcanist Doan] at the end of the Library and open Doan's Strongbox behind him for The Scarlet Key [CI7146,1 The Scarlet Key] [G83.9,31.3 Tirisfal Glades]
[OC]|cffffcc00Loot (Doan):|r |cff66ff66Mantle of Doan|r (cloth shoulders +6 Int +8 Spi +7 spell damage, req 34, ~32%) - roll: it beats Batwing Mantle on the weights. Robe of Doan - pass. Library Walkers and Band of Crimson Light from the wing's trash and bosses - pass

[OC]|cffffffffArmory|r  -  mobs 35-40 in the DB: Soldiers and Conjurors 35-36, Evokers, Guardsmen and Protectors 36-37; Herod, the Scarlet Champion, 40 elite at the end
|cFFFF0000GROUP 5|r Enter the Armory wing (the Scarlet Key may be needed for its door, unverified) [G83.9,31.3 Tirisfal Glades]
Kill [TAR3975 Herod] [QC1053,3] [G83.9,31.3 Tirisfal Glades]
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Loot (Herod):|r |cff66ff66Ravager|r (2H axe 37.3 dps, req 37, ~25%) - roll: if it drops it is your best two-hander until chapter 39c, ahead of Defender of Dalaran and Rock Pulverizer (chapter 35). Herod's Shoulder and Raging Berserker's Helm are mail (not until 40) - pass
[OC]|cffffcc00Cathedral:|r not this trip. It is left for chapter 39c at level 39-40, when the route passes Southshore and the crater again. In the Name of the Light (1053) stays in your log until then (Loksey and Herod done, Mograine and Whitemane open); keep The Scarlet Key from Doan's Strongbox for its door
[OC]|cffffcc00Leaving:|r walk out of the Armory. Do NOT hearth: it would drop you in Desolace, and the hand-ins are south

[OC]|cffffffffHome|r  -  the same swim back south, Olvek in the crater, then Southshore and the flight to Ironforge
Run south-west across Tirisfal, off the roads, and swim south across Lordamere Lake to the Dalaran crater [G18,72 Alterac Mountains]
[OC]|cffffcc00Gear (Past Due):|r take the |cff66ff66Knucklebound Thimble|r (ring +8 Sta, 43s 99c) for an empty ring slot or the vendor; Salve and Salvation is an off-hand you do not use with a two-hander (43s 83c)
At [TAR264265 Magus Olvek], [QT96800] (2,850 XP + 45s) [G9.8,63.4 Alterac Mountains]
Back through the north-west pass and across the Hillsbrad Fields to Southshore, west of Tarren Mill [G33,42 Hillsbrad Foothills]
At [TAR2432 Darla Harris], |cFFfff8a3Fly to [F Ironforge]|r [G49.3,52.3 Hillsbrad Foothills]
[OC]|cffffcc00Gear (Mythology of the Titans):|r the Explorers' League Commendation (neck +9 Sta +9 Spi) is below Giantstone Medallion and the Thermaplugg Medal: wear it only if your neck is weaker, otherwise vendor it
At [TAR3979 Librarian Mae Paledust] in the Hall of Explorers, [QT1050] (3,550 XP) [G75.0,12.5 Ironforge]
[OC]|cffffcc00Check:|r handed in here: Down the Scarlet Path (1052), Past Due (96800) and Mythology of the Titans (1050). In the log for later chapters: In the Name of the Light (1053, Mograine and Whitemane open, to the Cathedral and Raleigh in 39c), The Coldbringer's Eye (96773, to Razorfen Downs in 39b and Lan'dalock in 39c), Storm, Earth, and Fire (79358), On the Lam (79235, chapter 37) and the other carries from chapter 27 (Ironband Wants You! 707 for chapter 35). Hearth = Nijel's Point. Next: chapter 35 starts here in Ironforge (Eldrun's training, then Gryth Thurden for Thelsamar)
[NX 36-38 Badlands]
